  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p> A combination of multiple rib fractures causes one side of your chest to essentially detach from the rest of the rib cage. Your diaphragm and other breathing muscles find it very hard to work under these conditions, with much grinding together of broken bone ends and ineffectual lung inflation being the result.</p> <p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Unconscious], although you’re strictly speaking awake, helpless and in great distress for the first Toughness Bonus turns before actually losing consciousness. Unless you receive Surgery within a day you’ll expire. Successful Surgery will still not prevent you from contracting Blood Rot due to being unable to cough properly to ventilate your lungs and prevent pneumonia. Should you survive you’ll be bedridden and helpless for 40+1d10 days while your chest pieces reconnect, and will afterwards gain @Condition[Fatigued] (1) permanently.</p>"
    },
